00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:54.850
<i>What should we do?</i>
<i>We're not used to facing adversity</i>

00:02:54.850 --> 00:02:59.980
<i>So our resolve's definitely not all there</i>

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:02.400
<i>Back then, we were just</i>

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:04.730
<i>Envious of others and</i>

00:03:04.730 --> 00:03:09.440
<i>Angry at something we couldn't see</i>

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:11.980
<i>We just kept glaring at the next step</i>

00:03:11.980 --> 00:03:14.350
<i>That we could've easily taken</i>

00:03:14.350 --> 00:03:19.350
<i>And it was eating away at us silently</i>

00:03:20.770 --> 00:03:23.150
<i>We were so scared that we went numb</i>

00:03:23.150 --> 00:03:25.560
<i>And our legs buckled from under us</i>

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:30.440
<i>We still can't forget the tears</i>
<i>that fell back then even now</i>

00:03:30.440 --> 00:03:35.230
<i>Even though we're so frail we might break,</i>
<i>we still continued to seek love</i>

00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:40.350
<i>We don't want to forget the reason</i>
<i>we're standing on this stage</i>

00:03:40.350 --> 00:03:45.150
<i>Because you're the one who made me stronger</i>

00:03:45.150 --> 00:03:49.600
<i>I give you this lovely ballad</i>
<i>within this beautiful attack</i>

00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:01.970
Fukuho Technical High School

00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:01.970
Fukuho Technical High School

00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:01.970
Fukuho Technical High School

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:02.100
Coach.

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:05.600
I edited the video of our
practice match with Kodzu High.

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:06.100
Episode 6: 'The Laughing King and Crybaby Jack'

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:06.850
Good work.

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:09.310
What'd you think about the match?

00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:14.310
Their blockers kept piling up on the left,
so Subaru kept getting blocked.

00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:17.310
We didn't actually lose any points,
but it still doesn't feel too great.

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:22.850
Could you reserve the
AV room for us on Saturday?

00:04:22.850 --> 00:04:24.060
Yes, sir.

00:04:26.190 --> 00:04:30.100
Hey, Ochi. About having someone
take over as the manager...

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:32.400
I'm not retiring yet.

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:35.730
Are you sure? Aren't you going to college?

00:04:35.730 --> 00:04:38.730
I'll keep doing my job
as long as Subaru keeps winning.

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:42.590
"Faculty Room"

00:04:40.810 --> 00:04:44.480
I got hurt the summer
of my first year in high school.

00:04:46.270 --> 00:04:48.310
I got hurt during practice.

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:53.400
My dream of going to the same high school

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:56.230
as Fukui's Charismatic Player Subaru Mimura

00:04:56.230 --> 00:05:00.150
and going to the nationals with him ended up...

00:05:07.770 --> 00:05:10.190
The manager?

00:05:10.190 --> 00:05:12.230
Our third year Kida's gonna be
concentrating on entrance exams,

00:05:12.230 --> 00:05:14.600
so as soon as the Inter-High is done,
I want them to retire

00:05:14.600 --> 00:05:16.980
so they can concentrate on their studies.

00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:20.350
I'm not asking you to be the
manager because you got hurt.

00:05:20.350 --> 00:05:23.650
Ochi, it's because I think
you're perfect for the job.

00:05:25.940 --> 00:05:29.350
Seriously? The manager?

00:05:29.350 --> 00:05:31.770
Ochi, you come here, too?

00:05:31.770 --> 00:05:33.980
How're you doing?

00:05:33.980 --> 00:05:36.440
Mimura...

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:37.440
Wait, what?

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:39.690
Come on, don't call me Mimura.

00:05:39.690 --> 00:05:40.940
My name's Subaru.

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:44.100
So call me Subaru. Everyone else does.

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:45.560
Oh... Right.

00:05:45.560 --> 00:05:49.350
I messed up my knees back in middle school, too.

00:05:49.350 --> 00:05:52.230
Had surgery on both sides.

00:05:52.230 --> 00:05:56.810
Surgeries? But when? You've basically
been in all the tournaments.

00:05:56.810 --> 00:06:01.400
Hm... The second one was the
spring break right before my third year.

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:04.310
The first one was a year before that, I think.

00:06:04.310 --> 00:06:06.270
And you're... still coming here?

00:06:06.270 --> 00:06:08.650
Today was just a routine checkup.

00:06:08.650 --> 00:06:11.940
They told me I'd be fine
as long as I take good care of them.

00:06:11.940 --> 00:06:14.810
More importantly,
you're in a rough spot right now.

00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:20.310
Well, they told me I'd be doing
physical therapy for four months.

00:06:20.310 --> 00:06:22.270
That's long.

00:06:22.270 --> 00:06:26.310
But if all goes well,
you'll make the Newcomer Match.

00:06:26.310 --> 00:06:28.100
The Newcomer Match?

00:06:28.100 --> 00:06:31.980
Even if I get better, I have no shot
at being on the starting lineup.

00:06:31.980 --> 00:06:33.270
Anyone's got a shot--

00:06:33.270 --> 00:06:34.770
No, they don't.

00:06:34.770 --> 00:06:36.400
I'm sure you don't know how it feels, Mimura.

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:40.480
Having the coach ask if you want to be
the manager the second you get hurt.

00:06:40.480 --> 00:06:43.770
That'd never happen to you,
so you'd never understand how I feel.

00:06:43.770 --> 00:06:45.730
Ochi, wait. Hey!

00:06:50.520 --> 00:06:52.440
I can't believe I snapped at him.

00:07:08.850 --> 00:07:11.190
Hey, your knees!

00:07:11.190 --> 00:07:16.270
Why're you leaving?
We were in the middle of talking.

00:07:16.270 --> 00:07:18.810
S-Sorry...

00:07:18.810 --> 00:07:29.100
I-I think you're really amazing.
So I didn't mean what I said earlier.

00:07:29.100 --> 00:07:33.310
I-I just can't think the same way you do.

00:07:33.310 --> 00:07:39.480
I know I just need to concentrate on
my physical therapy and continue playing.

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:44.810
But I couldn't help but think about
stuff and just got depressed.

00:07:44.810 --> 00:07:49.480
You regret coming to Fukuho?

00:07:49.480 --> 00:07:52.230
But right now, there's no other school in Fukui

00:07:52.230 --> 00:07:56.020
that can get to nationals other than Fukuho.

00:07:56.020 --> 00:07:59.850
And that's why you chose Fukuho, right?

00:08:01.270 --> 00:08:04.810
Why not give being a manager a try?

00:08:04.810 --> 00:08:05.650
Huh?

00:08:05.650 --> 00:08:09.440
If you're gonna mope around,
give being the manager a shot.

00:08:09.440 --> 00:08:11.400
You'll definitely be on the bench then!

00:08:11.400 --> 00:08:14.520
What? The hell kind of logic is that?

00:08:14.520 --> 00:08:19.850
Ochi, don't you wanna go to the
center court at the Spring Tournament?

00:08:19.850 --> 00:08:23.690
Well? Do you want to go or not?

00:08:23.690 --> 00:08:26.810
O-Of course, I do.

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:28.060
But...

00:08:28.060 --> 00:08:30.350
Then quit your moping

00:08:30.350 --> 00:08:33.900
and leave your three years in high school to me.

00:08:33.900 --> 00:08:38.190
I'll make sure you get to be
the manager in the center court.

00:08:38.190 --> 00:08:39.940
Just imagine it.

00:08:39.940 --> 00:08:42.810
Everyone's gonna notice you,
and it'll be awesome!

00:08:46.770 --> 00:08:48.480
So you know how the girl manager from Kodzu

00:08:48.480 --> 00:08:51.730
came to get Subaru- <i>senpai</i> 's autograph?

00:08:51.730 --> 00:08:55.480
Apparently that tiny girl's
their captain's girlfriend.

00:08:55.480 --> 00:08:57.980
Oh, the girl with the the ponytail.

00:08:57.980 --> 00:08:59.850
She seemed really pleasant.

00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:01.440
That's unforgivable, isn't it?!

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:03.940
That's why coed schools are weaker.

00:09:03.940 --> 00:09:06.850
Kohei, just in case you forgot, we're coed, too.

00:09:06.850 --> 00:09:10.810
Senpai, I wish we had a girl manager, too.

00:09:10.810 --> 00:09:12.730
It wouldn't hurt if we got a little weaker.

00:09:12.730 --> 00:09:16.350
If you want a girl manager so bad,
go to Kodzu High.

00:09:16.350 --> 00:09:18.810
O-Ochi- <i>senpai</i> ...

00:09:18.810 --> 00:09:20.560
You can sit here, Senpai.

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:22.850
I've got study hall next, so I'm gonna go.

00:09:22.850 --> 00:09:24.400
Me, too.

00:09:24.400 --> 00:09:28.770
Tomoki, I made sure the tape and
cooling spray will get here on Saturday.

00:09:28.770 --> 00:09:30.190
Try to hold up until then.

00:09:30.190 --> 00:09:32.350
Right. You got it.

00:09:32.350 --> 00:09:35.940
Seriously, we can't get any weaker.

00:09:35.940 --> 00:09:37.600
Did you forget our goal?

00:09:37.600 --> 00:09:40.560
Sorry... I'll settle with you, Ochi- <i>senpai</i> .

00:09:40.560 --> 00:09:43.940
I mean, I prefer you,
Ochi- <i>senpai</i> ! You're the best!

00:09:43.940 --> 00:09:48.060
Well, none of us are expecting
you to comfort us, Ochi.

00:09:48.060 --> 00:09:50.810
No one wants to imagine you
having a high-pitched voice.

00:09:50.810 --> 00:09:53.060
Well, I'm sorry to disappoint.

00:09:53.060 --> 00:09:55.770
Ochi has his own job to do.

00:09:55.770 --> 00:09:57.980
Subaru's exactly right.

00:09:57.980 --> 00:09:59.850
Ever since Ochi became our manager,

00:09:59.850 --> 00:10:02.060
we've been able to dissect
our opponents even better.

00:10:02.060 --> 00:10:04.650
And he puts it on video so it's easy to watch.

00:10:04.650 --> 00:10:07.310
I'm sorry for what I said.

00:10:07.310 --> 00:10:11.230
Kohei, I want some dessert.

00:10:11.230 --> 00:10:13.350
You got it! I'll go buy you something.

00:10:14.560 --> 00:10:16.400
I want the Big Chocolate Pudding.

00:10:16.400 --> 00:10:17.900
If they don't have that, whatever is fine.

00:10:17.900 --> 00:10:19.810
I will get it without fail!

00:10:21.480 --> 00:10:26.400
Guess the second years don't feel
like they need to lead the team yet.

00:10:26.400 --> 00:10:28.480
Subaru's presence is just too huge.

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:33.980
Everyone younger than us playing
volleyball is a fan of Subaru.

00:10:33.980 --> 00:10:35.900
What did you want to talk about?

00:10:35.900 --> 00:10:37.350
PM classes are starting soo--

00:10:37.350 --> 00:10:38.850
Subaru.

00:10:38.850 --> 00:10:42.150
Our match with Kodzu High
the other day... What was that?

00:10:42.150 --> 00:10:43.730
What do you mean?

00:10:43.730 --> 00:10:45.770
You weren't with it at all.

00:10:45.770 --> 00:10:47.190
Are you taking this seriously?

00:10:47.190 --> 00:10:50.230
I know you're trying to ignore
what happened at nationals,

00:10:50.230 --> 00:10:52.310
so I won't pry about that, but...

00:10:52.310 --> 00:10:55.850
I'm not ignoring it. I'm just not into it.

00:10:55.850 --> 00:10:57.650
It's not like that'll make Fukuho win.

00:10:57.650 --> 00:11:02.310
But we're still carrying Fukui!
You're Fukui's ace, too!

00:11:02.310 --> 00:11:04.400
Fukui's ace?

00:11:04.400 --> 00:11:07.400
Basically the first thing outta anyone's mouth

00:11:07.400 --> 00:11:10.270
at the Inter-High venue
is usually, "Where's Fukui?"

00:11:10.270 --> 00:11:12.900
Don't let something that dumb get you down.

00:11:12.900 --> 00:11:16.020
If we make it to the center court,
we'll have more fame than we'd ever want.

00:11:16.020 --> 00:11:20.060
We just need to let everyone know where it is!

00:11:20.060 --> 00:11:23.850
Well, look at you, whippin' everyone into shape.

00:11:23.850 --> 00:11:27.190
Hard to imagine you're the same kid
who was crying at the hospital.

00:11:28.520 --> 00:11:30.900
Sorry, I take that back.

00:11:32.770 --> 00:11:34.350
It's fine.

00:11:34.350 --> 00:11:37.770
You can say whatever you want to me.

00:11:37.770 --> 00:11:39.190
Let's go to class.

00:11:41.150 --> 00:11:42.310
Ochi.

00:11:44.100 --> 00:11:48.350
You wanna go to the center court
at the Spring Tournament?

00:11:48.350 --> 00:11:50.600
I told you earlier.

00:11:50.600 --> 00:11:52.600
Then ask me properly

00:11:52.600 --> 00:11:57.060
to make you the manager
at the Spring Tournament.

00:11:57.060 --> 00:12:00.810
Yeah. You're the one who gave me this dream.

00:12:00.810 --> 00:12:06.940
So you damn well better get me to the
center court at the Spring Tournament.

00:12:06.940 --> 00:12:08.230
You got it!

00:12:19.560 --> 00:12:22.810
We made it to the best 16 at Inter-High,

00:12:22.810 --> 00:12:25.190
but we're going to work even harder as a team

00:12:25.190 --> 00:12:29.560
to get even higher at the Spring Tournament.

00:12:29.560 --> 00:12:34.020
That was Subaru Mimura, the captain
of Fukuho Tech's boys volleyball team.

00:12:34.020 --> 00:12:35.350
Thank you very much.

00:12:35.350 --> 00:12:36.400
Subaru.

00:12:36.400 --> 00:12:38.770
Fukuho's probably gonna
be on top again this year,

00:12:38.770 --> 00:12:40.600
but are there any teams you're looking out for?

00:12:40.600 --> 00:12:42.560
Teams I'm looking out for?

00:12:42.560 --> 00:12:43.600
Oh, you haven't heard?

00:12:43.600 --> 00:12:47.150
I heard that Seiin's putting together
an interesting team this year.

00:12:47.150 --> 00:12:50.650
Seiin? The team that withdrew
at the Fall Tournament semi-finals?

00:12:50.650 --> 00:12:52.190
Yeah, them.

00:12:52.190 --> 00:12:54.520
Their setter's only a first-year still,

00:12:54.520 --> 00:12:57.850
but he was on a team that made it
to the best six back in Tokyo.

00:12:57.850 --> 00:12:59.350
Huh...

00:12:59.350 --> 00:13:00.940
Tokyo, eh?

00:13:00.940 --> 00:13:03.810
Oh? Bet you are interested, Subaru.

00:13:03.810 --> 00:13:08.150
Fukuho better stay on their toes,
or someone might just take their spot.

00:13:08.150 --> 00:13:11.480
It gets boring if Fukuho's always a shoe in.

00:13:13.940 --> 00:13:15.440
The hell was that?

00:13:15.440 --> 00:13:20.100
If it's more interesting if we lose,
then don't bother interviewing us.

00:13:20.100 --> 00:13:21.770
Seiin...

00:13:21.770 --> 00:13:24.400
Looks like they're catching some wind.

00:13:24.400 --> 00:13:28.020
The current captain at Seiin is Oda, right?

00:13:28.020 --> 00:13:30.350
I don't remember them being that good.

00:13:30.350 --> 00:13:33.350
Yeah. Up until the
Inter-High qualifiers, that is.

00:13:33.350 --> 00:13:36.310
But they randomly popped up
at the Fall Tournament.

00:13:36.310 --> 00:13:39.020
They've got a first year ace and setter duo.

00:13:39.020 --> 00:13:42.980
The kid who made a best-six team
in Tokyo is a first-year named Haijima.

00:13:42.980 --> 00:13:44.480
He's was a setter for a Tokyo middle school team

00:13:44.480 --> 00:13:49.190
that made it to the best four
at the Kanto Tournament.

00:13:49.190 --> 00:13:52.560
Apparently, he was a second year in
middle school when he made it to the best six.

00:13:52.560 --> 00:13:55.560
The best six when he was
a second year in middle school...

00:13:55.560 --> 00:13:59.350
Subaru, you're one of
Fukui's greatest treasures.

00:13:59.350 --> 00:14:03.190
I'm proud to be able to have you on our team.

00:14:03.190 --> 00:14:05.850
Haijima's two years younger than you,

00:14:05.850 --> 00:14:09.900
but I believe he's the other genius
that Fukui has right now.

00:14:13.900 --> 00:14:16.100
He managed a quick during
that rally at the end there.

00:14:16.100 --> 00:14:17.690
And a B pass.

00:14:17.690 --> 00:14:19.940
That setter's got some balls.

00:14:25.400 --> 00:14:29.400
So Seiin withdrew from the semi-finals
at the Fall Tournament for some reason,

00:14:29.400 --> 00:14:31.690
but their coach was definitely
at the coaches' meeting

00:14:31.690 --> 00:14:34.190
for the prefectural qualifiers.

00:14:34.190 --> 00:14:35.770
They're gonna be there.

00:14:35.770 --> 00:14:38.400
They have five players
that are over 180 cm high.

00:14:38.400 --> 00:14:40.900
Where the hell they'd pop up from?

00:14:40.900 --> 00:14:43.940
The members of Seiin that were
at the Fall Tournament are...

00:14:43.940 --> 00:14:46.940
On the left, they've got their
#1 Oda and their #7 Kuroba.

00:14:46.940 --> 00:14:50.100
Oda's the captain and 163 cm,

00:14:50.100 --> 00:14:53.150
but Kuroba's a first year and is 184 cm tall.

00:14:53.150 --> 00:14:57.060
On the right, they've got their #4 Kanno.
He's a second year and 181 cm.

00:14:57.060 --> 00:15:02.400
Their middle blockers are their #2 and #10,
and they're 193 cm and 187 cm.

00:15:02.400 --> 00:15:05.690
Their #2, Aoki; I'm sure
everyone's seen him before.

00:15:05.690 --> 00:15:07.480
Their #10 is a second year named Okuma

00:15:07.480 --> 00:15:09.100
and this is the first I'm seeing him, too.

00:15:09.100 --> 00:15:13.230
And their #8 that got that
service ace must be their setter.

00:15:13.230 --> 00:15:16.770
Yeah. Not only can he pull of spike serves,

00:15:16.770 --> 00:15:20.900
he's a tall setter sitting at 181 cm.
He's Haijima and a first year.

00:15:20.900 --> 00:15:25.270
I have to wonder... Why didn't
this kid come to our school?

00:15:25.270 --> 00:15:28.900
Coach, you always go to the
middle-school tournaments, don't you?

00:15:28.900 --> 00:15:30.350
Yeah.

00:15:30.350 --> 00:15:34.690
I had my eye on Haijima, too,
after seeing him play.

00:15:34.690 --> 00:15:37.980
But honestly, I just didn't know
how to fit him into this team

00:15:37.980 --> 00:15:42.400
when Subaru was gonna be a third year.

00:15:42.400 --> 00:15:45.980
A part of me did want to see what he'd pull off

00:15:45.980 --> 00:15:48.560
if he was on the same team as Subaru, but...

00:15:48.560 --> 00:15:52.230
Are you saying we're not enough, Coach?

00:15:52.230 --> 00:15:54.850
Nah, that's not what I meant.

00:15:54.850 --> 00:15:59.520
I'm sure that's what some people think.
At least, the media people.

00:15:59.520 --> 00:16:04.190
In the last seven years, we're the
only team that's made nationals.

00:16:04.190 --> 00:16:07.190
They're probably thinking that,
if some team beats us,

00:16:07.190 --> 00:16:10.520
they're just gonna
somehow make it to the top.

00:16:10.520 --> 00:16:11.900
Subaru- <i>senpai</i> ?

00:16:16.400 --> 00:16:19.560
Sorry about that. That was my fault.

00:16:19.560 --> 00:16:24.230
We'll keep an eye on Seiin,
but we don't need to get our guard up.

00:16:24.230 --> 00:16:26.310
We're gonna start practice at nine.

00:16:26.310 --> 00:16:27.560
Right.

00:16:49.560 --> 00:16:51.690
O-Ochi- <i>senpai</i> ...

00:16:51.690 --> 00:16:55.980
You seem well considering you bailed
on practice because of a stomach ache.

00:16:55.980 --> 00:17:00.060
I-I thought I'd go watch Seiin practice.

00:17:00.060 --> 00:17:05.730
You've got better things to do than worry
about some team we may never play.

00:17:05.730 --> 00:17:08.400
Well, yeah, but...

00:17:10.100 --> 00:17:12.060
I'll go, too.

00:17:12.060 --> 00:17:15.850
I can't have you distracted by what's
going on another court at qualifiers.

00:17:17.770 --> 00:17:23.100
Excuse me. Do you know where the
boys volleyball team is practicing?

00:17:23.100 --> 00:17:24.850
Do we even have a boys volleyball team?

00:17:24.850 --> 00:17:27.190
We probably have one.

00:17:27.190 --> 00:17:30.480
Probably in the gym
or one of the courts outside.

00:17:31.650 --> 00:17:35.730
We're not talking about middle school
PE class. The courts outside? Really?

00:17:35.730 --> 00:17:37.400
Well, let's go take a look.

00:17:37.400 --> 00:17:42.190
I'll go check the gym.
You go check out the courts outside.

00:17:42.190 --> 00:17:43.270
Okay.

00:17:48.230 --> 00:17:51.100
Excuse me. Where's the boys' volleyball...

00:17:51.100 --> 00:17:56.520
They're outside today. Oh, but I
think they'll wrapping it up soon.

00:17:56.520 --> 00:17:59.440
They're letting us use the gym after 6 PM.

00:17:59.440 --> 00:18:01.850
They don't get to practice in the gym every day?

00:18:01.850 --> 00:18:05.520
Nope. Both the boys and girls volleyball
teams have tournaments soon,

00:18:05.520 --> 00:18:10.650
so as soon as the other clubs leave,
we can use the gym until 7:30.

00:18:10.650 --> 00:18:14.270
Um, are you the manager for the girls team?

00:18:14.270 --> 00:18:17.020
Nope, I'm on the boys team.

00:18:17.020 --> 00:18:21.440
If you want to check out the court outside,
I'll tell you how to get there.

00:18:18.520 --> 00:18:21.440
This must the second year Kanno.

00:18:21.440 --> 00:18:25.120
He's a year younger than me.
I didn't have to be so formal with him then.

00:18:23.900 --> 00:18:26.020
What? Say that again, you punk!

00:18:26.020 --> 00:18:27.650
I dare you to say that again!

00:18:27.650 --> 00:18:29.270
The hell did you just say?

00:18:29.270 --> 00:18:31.900
Kohei! What're you doing?!

00:18:29.270 --> 00:18:30.810
I'll say it as many time as you want!

00:18:30.810 --> 00:18:31.900
Take that back!

00:18:31.900 --> 00:18:33.310
Senpai!

00:18:33.310 --> 00:18:35.270
Kohei! What're you--

00:18:35.270 --> 00:18:37.230
Ochi- <i>senpai</i> .

00:18:37.230 --> 00:18:44.060
He said that Fukuho must not be that
big a deal if we're here snooping around.

00:18:44.060 --> 00:18:47.150
I didn't say you weren't a big deal.

00:18:47.150 --> 00:18:50.100
I just said you guys must've
finally been humbled!

00:18:50.100 --> 00:18:52.730
What, you bastard?!

00:18:52.730 --> 00:18:55.020
Oh? And who are you?

00:18:55.020 --> 00:18:58.600
I'm a third year and my name is Ochi.
I'm Fukuho's manager.

00:18:58.600 --> 00:19:04.270
Manager? It can't be fun being
a guy manager on a guys' team.

00:19:04.270 --> 00:19:08.850
Who do you think you're talking to?!

00:19:05.270 --> 00:19:08.850
That's enough.

00:19:08.850 --> 00:19:10.230
Aoki?

00:19:10.230 --> 00:19:14.650
You causing all this fuss, Ochi?

00:19:15.850 --> 00:19:21.690
I've got great footage of your
careless boy's violent actions.

00:19:21.690 --> 00:19:24.810
Would be a shame if this footage
was ever made public.

00:19:24.810 --> 00:19:29.810
Th-That's messed up! That guy
on your team started all this!

00:19:29.810 --> 00:19:31.350
If you guys weren't so rude--

00:19:31.350 --> 00:19:32.900
That's enough!

00:19:32.900 --> 00:19:37.350
S-Subaru, why--

00:19:39.730 --> 00:19:44.020
Damn. I almost died on that hill.

00:19:44.020 --> 00:19:45.150
We're sorry!

00:19:45.150 --> 00:19:48.190
Could we just keep this between us?

00:19:48.190 --> 00:19:51.600
I can't let my team get in trouble.

00:19:51.600 --> 00:19:54.350
I'm truly sorry that my teammates were rude.

00:19:54.350 --> 00:19:58.560
So please, I'm begging you, Oda. For my sake.

00:19:58.560 --> 00:20:00.480
Subaru, don't!

00:20:00.480 --> 00:20:01.560
If someone's gonna apologize, we'll do it.

00:20:01.560 --> 00:20:05.310
Shut up! There's no point
in you guys apologizing.

00:20:05.310 --> 00:20:06.600
Please, Oda.

00:20:06.600 --> 00:20:08.900
If we're not able to play
over something as silly as this,

00:20:08.900 --> 00:20:10.230
we'll never live it down.

00:20:10.230 --> 00:20:13.190
If Fukuho's record comes
to a halt because of this,

00:20:13.190 --> 00:20:17.020
I'll never be able to face our seniors again.

00:20:17.020 --> 00:20:18.770
I-I'm sorry!

00:20:18.770 --> 00:20:20.650
I'm the only one to blame here!

00:20:20.650 --> 00:20:22.770
If we can settle this
by throwing me off the team...

00:20:22.770 --> 00:20:24.900
H-Hey, wait a sec.

00:20:24.900 --> 00:20:29.940
This isn't that big of a deal. Please, stand up.

00:20:29.940 --> 00:20:32.940
Mimura, I don't want any trouble, either.

00:20:32.940 --> 00:20:36.850
And I apologize for whatever
our idiot said, too.

00:20:36.850 --> 00:20:39.230
Okuma!

00:20:39.230 --> 00:20:42.400
Sorry about that, Fukuho.

00:20:42.400 --> 00:20:45.060
Aoki, delete your video.

00:20:45.060 --> 00:20:47.810
Don't worry, I wasn't recording.

00:20:50.020 --> 00:20:52.020
We owe you.

00:20:52.020 --> 00:20:54.350
You came to see our practice, didn't you?

00:20:54.350 --> 00:20:56.350
Then come on.

00:20:56.350 --> 00:21:01.690
Nah, we settled things for now,
so I'm gonna drag these two home.

00:21:01.690 --> 00:21:04.730
But instead...

00:21:04.730 --> 00:21:07.060
Why don't we do a practice match?

00:21:09.520 --> 00:21:13.730
Well? I think it's a great idea.

00:21:13.730 --> 00:21:15.190
That's him.

00:21:15.190 --> 00:21:19.150
He's the other genius that Fukui has right now.

00:21:19.150 --> 00:21:22.440
That's Haijima.

00:21:22.440 --> 00:21:24.520
Sure, why not?

00:21:24.520 --> 00:21:27.060
There's no need to be stingy.

00:21:27.060 --> 00:21:30.900
Looks like they're super curious about us.

00:21:31.980 --> 00:21:37.600
<i>I don't want a wish to end as just a wish</i>

00:21:39.190 --> 00:21:44.810
<i>But I know I'm going to live with that feeling</i>

00:21:46.440 --> 00:21:53.650
<i>And as I toss and turn</i>

00:21:53.650 --> 00:21:57.690
<i>The azure world smiles upon me</i>

00:22:02.650 --> 00:22:10.060
<i>The knife made up of words from my friend</i>

00:22:10.060 --> 00:22:16.980
<i>Still lingers inside my head today</i>

00:22:16.980 --> 00:22:23.150
<i>You glared up at the clouds high in the sky</i>

00:22:24.310 --> 00:22:29.600
<i>And near your house, the horizon undulated</i>

00:22:31.480 --> 00:22:37.060
<i>I don't want a wish to end as just a wish</i>

00:22:38.690 --> 00:22:44.230
<i>But I know I'm going to live with that feeling</i>

00:22:45.980 --> 00:22:53.150
<i>And as I toss and turn</i>

00:22:53.150 --> 00:23:01.310
<i>The azure world stabs me strongly in the back</i>
